1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,440
I remember my 30 th birthday about 2 and 1 2 years ago I was feeling stuck uninspired stagnant.
我记得大约两年半前过三十岁生日时，我觉得自己卡住了，没有灵感，停滞不前。

2
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:12,720
It was like I loved my life I I very grateful for the life that I was living and I was blessed.
当时的感觉是，我热爱自己的生活，也非常感激当时的生活，觉得自己很幸运。

3
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:18,870
But I was just I don't want to say bored but I I just the life I envisioned I wasn't necessarily living.
但我就是……我不想说无聊，可我当时并没有真正过上自己想象中的生活。

4
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:25,119
I knew I could do more I knew I could be more I just knew I could elevate to a certain level.
我知道自己可以做得更多、变得更好，也知道自己可以提升到某个水平。

5
00:00:25,119 --> 00:00:31,600
And it was then that I realized I have to make some changes within myself in order to change everything else around me.
就是在那个时候，我意识到，要改变周围的一切，我得先从自身做出一些改变。

6
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:35,360
And in order to do that I had to start my self improvement journey.
而为了做到这一点，我必须开始自己的自我提升之旅。

7
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:39,280
And I mean I think we're always evolving working on ourselves and changing.
我的意思是，我觉得我们一直都在发展、改善自身，也在改变。

8
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:48,320
But when you actively make the decision to improve it's the foundation of success foundation of confidence of a beautiful life really.
但当你主动决定提升自己时，她认为这就是成功、自信，以及美好生活的基础。

9
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:53,520
And I think for a lot of us when we think of self improvement we think self help books or podcasts.
我想，很多人一提到自我提升，就会想到自助类书籍或播客。

10
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:55,920
And all of those things are great they're very very helpful.
那些东西都很好，非常非常有帮助。

11
00:00:55,920 --> 00:01:05,439
But when you really want to improve yourself when you really want to change your life it's all about taking real intentional action to become the best version of you.
但当你真的想提升自己、改变生活时，关键在于采取切实、有意识的行动，成为最好的自己。

12
00:01:05,439 --> 00:01:10,960
When you commit to self improvement it builds confidence you attract better relationships.
她认为，投入自我提升会建立自信，也会吸引更好的关系。

13
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:15,520
You improve the relationships that you have the relationship that you have with yourself.
你会改善现有的关系，也会改善自己与自己的关系。

14
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:20,320
You improve your discipline and and your focus your habits and productivity.
你会提升自律和专注，改善习惯与效率。

15
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:24,720
And all of those things create a life that is filled with purpose and joy.
她认为，这些事情会共同创造充满目标感与喜悦的生活。

16
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:30,240
Now the biggest shift for me happened when I realized that my future is in my hands.
对我而言，最大的转变发生在我意识到未来掌握在自己手中的时候。

17
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:35,840
Sure life is unpredictable and we live in a world where there are a lot of things that we don't have control over.
当然，生活难以预测，我们所在的世界里有很多事情不在自己的控制之中。

18
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:41,839
But one of the things that you have control over are your habits your day to day is in your control.
但你能掌控的事情之一就是习惯，你的日常生活可以由你自己掌握。

19
00:01:41,839 --> 00:01:45,600
And the habits that you build today will create the life that you live tomorrow.
她认为，你今天建立的习惯会塑造明天的生活。

20
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:49,680
So the first area I want to talk to you about today and it's the most important in my opinion.
所以，今天我想先聊的第一个方面，在我看来也是最重要的。

21
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:58,320
This I would consider to be the domino effect area this will affect everything else I talk to you about today but it is your mindset.
我把它视为会产生多米诺效应的领域，会影响今天谈到的其他一切；它就是你的心态。

22
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:05,199
Your thoughts shape your reality if you believe you can achieve and I know that kind of sounds corny but it's very very true.
她说，思想会塑造现实，相信自己就能有所成就；她知道这听起来有点老套，但她非常认同。

23
00:02:05,199 --> 00:02:11,760
You have to start feeding yourself with empowering positive beliefs around you and your future.
你得开始用关于自己和未来的积极、有力量的信念来滋养自己。

24
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:18,400
And that happens with growth mindset and a fixed mindset so you have people who have growth mindsets and people who have fixed mindset.
这就涉及成长型心态和固定型心态；有些人持成长型心态，有些人持固定型心态。

25
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:27,279
A fixed mindset focuses on fear doubt procrastination feixed mindset feels oh this is what I'm born into so this is where I have to stay.
她把固定型心态描述为关注恐惧、怀疑与拖延，并觉得：我生来如此，所以只能停留在这里。

26
00:02:27,279 --> 00:02:37,360
Versus having a growth mindset people with a growth mindset understand that skills intelligence routines habits all of those things can be learned.
相比之下，她认为有成长型心态的人会明白，技能、智力、作息和习惯等都可以学习培养。

27
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:42,400
Having a growth mindset opens the door to learning resilience success.
她认为，成长型心态会为学习、韧性和成功打开大门。

28
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:50,080
You have to reframe negative thinking going from oh I can't do this to I'm learning and I'll get better at it.
你需要重新看待消极想法，把“我做不到”改成“我正在学习，而且会越来越好”。

29
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:56,720
Say that there's a challenge ahead and you're like you know what I'm not even going to start because I don't I don't think I'm going to finish.
比方说，前面有个挑战，你心想：算了，我连开始都不打算开始，因为我觉得自己完成不了。

30
00:02:56,720 --> 00:03:00,880
If that is the mindset that you have you won't even start so you will never know.
如果抱着这种心态，你连开始都不会，那就永远不会知道结果。

31
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:05,909
I think a lot of people are afraid of failing and they see failure as defeat.
我觉得很多人害怕失败，并把失败看成被打败。

32
00:03:05,919 --> 00:03:11,839
Or failure means you're insignificant or you're not meant to have this but failure is just a lesson.
或者觉得失败说明自己无足轻重、不配拥有这件事；但她把失败看作一堂课。

33
00:03:11,839 --> 00:03:16,160
In order to fail you have to start you're already successful by starting.
要经历失败，你得先开始；在她看来，愿意开始就已经是一种成功。

34
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:21,520
Speak positivity into yourself daily affirmations like those are really real.
对自己说积极的话，比如每日肯定语；她觉得这些确实有作用。

35
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:28,640
I wake up every single morning and I play positive affirmations so that I'm not worried about what happened yesterday.
我每天早上醒来都会播放积极肯定语，让自己不再担心昨天发生的事情。

36
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:34,320
Or anxious about what possibly could happen today focus on your mindset and you will change your life.
也不焦虑今天可能发生什么；她最后鼓励你关注心态，认为这会改变生活。
